use std
into gi_dynamic_check.amni

Imports: os, gfx, math, gfx.linalg, gfx.gltf, gfx.shapes, gfx.rt and gfx.scene3d. A standalone GPU program that checks dynamic global illumination (probes that follow moving and hidden objects, faster settling after changes, 16 lights with spot cones and one-sided rect lights) and prints one line per check, then "gi dynamic: ok" when all pass or "gi dynamic: FAILED" when any fails. These already exist; never define them here: `gfx::open_headless(w, h) bool`, `gfx::render_target(w, h, gfx::RGBA8)`, `gfx::translate(float3) gfx::mat4`, `gfx::flush()`, `shapes::material(rgb, metallic, roughness)`, `shapes::plane(half, m) int`, `shapes::cube(half float3, m) int`, `shapes::sphere(radius, around, down, m) int`, `shapes::sheet(n, o float3, u float3, v float3, m) int`, `s3d::add(asset) int`, `s3d::place(item, m)`, `s3d::items` (records with a bool field `visible`), `s3d::lights` (a list of `s3d::Light` records: `s3d::Light { pos: ..., range: ..., rgb: ..., kind: ..., dir: ..., cone: ..., width: ..., height: ..., .. }`, kind 0 point, 1 spot), `s3d::init(w, h) bool`, `s3d::render(target)`, `s3d::gi_read(out f32 list) bool` (fills the probe irradiance, four f32 per texel, rgb then 1), `s3d::gi_stats() int, int, real, real` (rebuilds, refits, the last refit's milliseconds, the last full build's milliseconds), `s3d::gi_rebuild()` (drops the probes and the ray-tracing scene so the next render builds both fresh), `rt::count() int`, `rt::tri_in` (f32 list, nine per triangle: three corners), `rt::hit(ox, oy, oz, dx, dy, dz, tmax) f32, int` (distance and triangle, -1 when nothing is hit within tmax), and the settings `s3d::gi_on`, `s3d::gi_dims` (three ints), `s3d::gi_rays`, `s3d::gi_updates_per_frame`, `s3d::gi_box`, `s3d::gi_box_lo`, `s3d::gi_box_hi`, `s3d::gi_refit` (bool), `s3d::gi_adaptive` (bool), `s3d::sun` (field `rgb`), `s3d::sky` (fields `ambient` and `draw`), `s3d::look` (field `bloom`) and `s3d::view` (an `s3d::Camera { eye, target, up, fov_y, near, far }`). Use `clock_ns()` (called bare, no module prefix) for timing.

Setup, 256 by 256: open headless (print "gi dynamic: skipped" and stop when it fails), sun rgb zero, sky ambient 0.2 and draw false, bloom 0, camera eye (0, 1.5, 3.5) looking at (0, 1, 0) with fov 1.0, near 0.05, far 50; `s3d::init(256, 256)` and a 256 by 256 render target. GI on with dims (8, 8, 8), 128 rays, one update per frame, the box on from (-2, 0, -2) to (2, 2.5, 2). The room: grey 0.7 roughness 0.9: a floor `shapes::plane(2.0, ...)` at the origin and four walls `shapes::cube` of half size (2, 1.25, 0.05) at (0, 1.25, -2) and (0, 1.25, 2), and of half size (0.05, 1.25, 2) at (-2, 1.25, 0) and (2, 1.25, 0); no ceiling, so the room is open to the sky. A red block (rgb (0.9, 0.05, 0.05), roughness 0.8) `shapes::cube` of half size (0.4, 0.4, 0.4) placed at (-1, 0.4, 0); keep its item. One point light at (0, 2.0, 0), range 6, rgb (3, 3, 3). Helpers: `frame()` renders once and flushes; `settle(n)` calls `frame` n times; `probes()` returns the probe irradiance read with `gi_read`; `err(a, b)` is the sum over every texel of the absolute differences of the r, g and b values of a and b over the sum of b's r, g and b (0 when that sum is 0); `fresh(n)` calls `gi_rebuild`, then `settle(n)`, and returns `probes()`.

D1 refit matches brute force: first `frame()` once so the scene is built, then read `gi_stats`; move the red block to (-1, 0.4, 0.5), `frame()`, to (0.5, 0.4, 0.5), `frame()`, to (0.5, 0.4, -0.8), `frame()`; the rebuild count from `gi_stats` must not have grown during these moves and the refit count must have grown by at least 3. Then shoot 20000 rays with a fixed linear congruential seed (state times 6364136223846793005 plus 1442695040888963407, wrapping, the top 24 bits over 2 to the 24 as a number in [0, 1)): origin uniform in the box (-1.9, 0.05, -1.9) to (1.9, 2.4, 1.9), direction a uniform unit vector (z uniform in [-1, 1], angle uniform in [0, 2 pi)), tmax 10. Brute force: over every triangle of `rt::tri_in` the nearest Moller-Trumbore hit with distance above 1e-6 and below tmax (no hit: distance tmax, triangle -1). A ray agrees when both miss, or both hit with distances within 1e-4. Pass when at least 99.9 % agree; detail the agreeing share with two decimals and the count of refits.

D2 no ghosts: put the block back at (-1, 0.4, 0), take `fresh(150)` as A0 (block inside); set the block's item `visible` false and take `fresh(150)` as R (the reference without the block); then set it visible again, take `fresh(150)` once more, hide it, `settle(60)` and take E. Same-history reference: hide the block, `fresh(150)`, `settle(60)` and take R2 (the probes rotate their rays by frame count, so R2 has the same ray history as E); the window noise is `err(R2, R)`. Pass when `err(E, R2)` is at most 0.03. Control "D2c stale scene keeps a ghost": the same with `gi_refit` false (show the block, `fresh(150)`, hide it, `settle(60)`), whose error against R2 must be above 0.03 and at least twice that of E against R2; then set `gi_refit` back to true. Detail both errors against R2 and the window noise with four decimals, and A0's error against R as the size of the change.

D3 settles faster: show the block, `fresh(150)`, hide it, then render frame by frame up to 300 frames and count the frames until `err(probes(), R)` is at most 0.05 (300 when never). Once with `gi_adaptive` true and once with it false (each starting from its own `fresh(150)` with the block shown). Pass when the adaptive count is at most half the plain count; detail both counts. Set `gi_adaptive` back to true and show the block.

D4 spot cones: remove the point light. Take `fresh(150)` with no lights as N. Add a spot (kind 1) at (0, 1.0, 0), dir (0, 1, 0), cone 0.3, range 6, rgb (8, 8, 8): `fresh(150)` is U (aimed up, out of the open top). Change its dir to (0, -1, 0): `fresh(150)` is D (aimed at the floor). The light added by the spot is the sum of the r, g and b over all texels of the probes minus that of N. Pass when U adds at most 0.05 times what D adds and D adds a positive amount; detail both added sums with three decimals (as shares of N's sum).

D4b rect lights shine one way: replace the spot by a rect light (kind 0, width 0.5, height 0.5) at (0, 2.4, 0), just under the wall tops so facing up it sees only open sky,, range 6, rgb (8, 8, 8), facing dir (0, 1, 0): `fresh(150)` is U; facing (0, -1, 0): `fresh(150)` is D. Pass with the same rule as D4; detail the same way.

D5 sixteen lights: remove all lights; add 16 point lights at (-1.5 + (i mod 4), 2.0, -1.5 + (i div 4)), range 3, where lights 0 to 7 have rgb (0, 0, 0) and lights 8 to 15 rgb (0.5, 0.5, 0.5); `fresh(150)` is S; take N from D4. Pass when S's sum is more than 1.2 times N's sum (lights beyond the eighth light the probes); detail the ratio with three decimals.

D6 refit cost: remove all lights and add back the point light at (0, 2, 0), range 6, rgb (3, 3, 3); add 10 spheres of radius 0.2 (48 around, 24 down, grey 0.7) at (-1.5 + 0.33 i, 1.5, 0); `gi_rebuild`, `frame()` once, then for 30 frames move sphere 0 to (-1.5, 1.5, 0.02 times the frame number) before each `frame()`. The mean refit milliseconds over those frames (from `gi_stats` after each frame) must be under 2 and under 0.25 times the full build milliseconds; detail the triangle count from `rt::count`, the mean refit and the build milliseconds with three decimals.

D7 refit scales with what moved: add a grid `shapes::sheet(n, o, u, v, m)` (it already exists) with n 400, o (-1.9, 2.3, -1.9), u (3.8, 0, 0), v (0, 0, 3.8), grey 0.7, at the origin (about 318000 triangles); `gi_rebuild`, `frame()` once, then for 30 frames move sphere 0 as in D6 before each `frame()`. Pass when the mean refit milliseconds is under 1 and under 0.05 times the full build milliseconds; detail the triangle count, the mean refit and the build milliseconds with three decimals.

`main()` sets up and runs D1, D2 (with D2c), D3, D4, D4b, D5, D6 and D7 in that order, each printing "PASS name (detail)" or "FAIL name (detail)", then the final line.
